Report a decoded surface as Ready

RequestSyncSurface marked a decoded surface VASurfaceDisplaying.
VA-API reserves Displaying for a surface being shown by an overlay
(vaPutSurface), which this driver never does. A finished decode is
VASurfaceReady.

GStreamer's va elements check vaQuerySurfaceStatus before deriving an
image and refuse anything that is not Ready (vasurfaceimage.c,
va_get_derive_image: "Surface not ready"). So every download to system
memory produced a NULL GstMemory:

  GStreamer-CRITICAL: gst_memory_unmap: assertion 'mem != NULL' failed

That broke vah264dec ! filesink, appsink, and the system-memory path into
glupload ("Failed to upload buffer"). ffmpeg never queries the status,
which is why nothing noticed. Every busy check here tests for
VASurfaceRendering, so nothing depended on Displaying.

---
diff --git a/src/surface.c b/src/surface.c
index f4893df..d546528 100644
--- a/src/surface.c
+++ b/src/surface.c
@@ -789,8 +789,16 @@ VAStatus RequestSyncSurface(VADriverContextP context, VASurfaceID surface_id)
 		goto error;
 	}
 
-	surface_object->status = VASurfaceDisplaying;
-	capture_surface->status = VASurfaceDisplaying;
+	/*
+	 * Decoded and dequeued: Ready. VASurfaceDisplaying means "being shown
+	 * by an overlay" (vaPutSurface), which this driver never does, and
+	 * GStreamer's va elements refuse to read a surface whose status is not
+	 * Ready (va_get_derive_image: "Surface not ready") -- every download to
+	 * system memory failed with a NULL GstMemory. Nothing here tests for
+	 * Displaying; the busy checks all test for Rendering.
+	 */
+	surface_object->status = VASurfaceReady;
+	capture_surface->status = VASurfaceReady;
 
 	/*
 	 * The decode failed on the picture that was just dequeued: the engine
